on-903d90ff-4e96-59f7-912a-24572f1e9b78"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/id #uuid "fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/math-academy-id "q-341777"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe $6$th cosine coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{a}_{6}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)={e}^{-{x}^{2}}$ and $L=5,$ the $6$th cosine coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{a}_{6}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/worked-solution "Recall that multiplying the argument of a function by $k\\ne 0$ represents the horizontal stretching of the corresponding graph by a factor of $\\frac{1}{k}.$\n\nNow, let $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x.$ Then, since $f(x)$ has a period of $2L,$ the function\n\n$$\ng(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\n$$\n\nmust have a period of $2L\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}=2\\pi .$ \n\nThe Fourier series of $g(s)$ is\n\n$$\ng(s)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns),\n$$\n\nwhere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ {a}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1 \\\\ {b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x$ and using the fact that $g(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s),$ we get the Fourier series of $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $6$th cosine coefficient of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $L=5$ and $f(x)={e}^{-{x}^{2}},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {\\int }_{-5}^{5}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{5}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-91327f8b-24a5-5a14-b72f-dc506b7dc1e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "91327f8b-24a5-5a14-b72f-dc506b7dc1e0"] ["answer-12dbb8fc-f8ae-55a2-b4d3-f92953f9c8be" :answer/id #uuid "12dbb8fc-f8ae-55a2-b4d3-f92953f9c8be"] ["answer-12dbb8fc-f8ae-55a2-b4d3-f92953f9c8be" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-12dbb8fc-f8ae-55a2-b4d3-f92953f9c8be" :answer/value "\\frac{L}{n\\pi }x"] ["answer-408b0c9c-4d17-5e7b-b2fd-1a3711a49bcf" :answer/id #uuid "408b0c9c-4d17-5e7b-b2fd-1a3711a49bcf"] ["answer-408b0c9c-4d17-5e7b-b2fd-1a3711a49bcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-408b0c9c-4d17-5e7b-b2fd-1a3711a49bcf" :answer/value "\\frac{nL}{\\pi }x"] ["answer-09a4dbf4-935c-5e5a-bfc2-9a1676fbd5fb" :answer/id #uuid "09a4dbf4-935c-5e5a-bfc2-9a1676fbd5fb"] ["answer-09a4dbf4-935c-5e5a-bfc2-9a1676fbd5fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-09a4dbf4-935c-5e5a-bfc2-9a1676fbd5fb" :answer/value "\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x"] ["answer-6e149a0