88ce292" :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e" :answer-field/key "field-5"] ["answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select] ["answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e" :answer-field/correct "answer-20a6260d-a64c-5771-b68c-fd4b972f15c7"] ["answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e" :answer-field/choices "answer-873e0942-50fd-5a7c-91e2-3b1957f1bed0"] ["answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e" :answer-field/choices "answer-20a6260d-a64c-5771-b68c-fd4b972f15c7"] ["answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e" :answer-field/choices "answer-23121dd1-c0fc-5a11-a114-b71f188cf2bf"] ["answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e" :answer-field/choices "answer-0b080894-e225-574e-b611-6de778384829"] ["answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e" :answer-field/choices "answer-16362305-1448-5d7f-841f-42942c9f6ad0"] ["answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e" :answer-field/choices "answer-84ff721d-5ea1-5783-b823-a370c88ce292"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-91327f8b-24a5-5a14-b72f-dc506b7dc1e0"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-27849c49-d7ae-5d00-af0d-9052f43cd943"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-85d4ff48-5bff-577d-8fcc-6da194224b88"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-20357d5e-1bc8-5dd7-8db6-94cde34f7b98"] ["question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f064fef8-a113-5d06-b95a-f4c517e2b24e"] [17592186221443 :knowledge-point/questions "question-fb364528-cf72-5941-b3b8-fc021ca9ace0"] ["question-bc08f5e3-6f0e-55df-87af-7552a06bb9df" :question/id #uuid "bc08f5e3-6f0e-55df-87af-7552a06bb9df"] ["question-bc08f5e3-6f0e-55df-87af-7552a06bb9df" :question/math-academy-id "q-341802"] ["question-bc08f5e3-6f0e-55df-87af-7552a06bb9df" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-3x+3$ for $x\\in [-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}"] ["question-bc08f5e3-6f0e-55df-87af-7552a06bb9df" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and $f(x)=-3x+3$ for $x\\in [-2,2).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(-3x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+3x]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {2}^{2}+3\\cdot 2)-(-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{2}+3\\cdot (-2))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(-12)) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-bc08f5e3-6f0e-55df-87af-7552a06bb9df" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b3e4d068-52a7-54b2-9f52-ab0c0b143b6e" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e4d068-52a7-54b2-9f52-ab0c0b143b6e"] ["answer-1f47cc34-1a40-54f8-8f21-1937b1207c8c" :answer/id #uuid "1f47cc34-1a40-54f8-8f21-1937b1207c8c"] ["answer-1f47cc34-1a40-54f8-8f21-1937b1207c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1f47cc34-1a40-54f8-8f21-1937b1207c8c" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-field-b3e4d068-52a7-54b2-9f52-ab0c0b143b6e" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-b3e4d068-52a7-54b2-9f52-ab0c0b143b6e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-b3e4d068-52a7-54b2-9f52-ab0c0b143b6e" :answer-field/correct "answer-1f47cc34-1a40-54f8-8f21-1937b1207c8c"] ["answer-field-b3e4d068-52a7-54b2-9f52-ab0c0b143b6e" :answer-field/choices "answer-1f47cc34-1a40-54f8-8f21-1937b1207c8c"] ["question-bc08f5e3-6f0e-55df-87af-7552a06bb9df" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b3e4d068-52a7-54b2-9f52-ab0c0b143b6e"] [17592186221444 :knowledge-point/questions "question-bc08f5e3-6f0e-55df-87af-7552a06bb9df"] ["question-14280c74-af6e-5d18-9712-69501b60ddc5" :question/id #uuid "14280c74-af6e-5d18-9712-69501b60ddc5"] ["question-14280c74-af6e-5d18-9712-69501b60ddc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-341830"] ["question-14280c74-af6e-5d18-9712-69501b60ddc5" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n}{2}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n}{2}x)\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of the $4\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5, & x\\in [0,2\\pi ) \\\\ -2, & x\\in [-2\\pi ,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis shown above. Find the exact value of ${b}_{3}.$\n\n${b}_{3}=$ {{field-1}}"] ["question-14280c74-af6e-5d18-9712-69501b60ddc5" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2\\pi .$ Also, $f(x)=5$ for $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $f(x)=-2$ for $x\\in [-2\\pi ,0).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{-2\\pi }^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{-2\\pi }^{0}(-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{2\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3}){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)]}_{-2\\pi }^{0}+\\frac{5}{2\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3}){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3\\pi ))-\\frac{5}{3\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }(1-(-1))-\\frac{5}{3\\pi }((-1)-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\pi }+\\frac{10}{3\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-14280c74-af6e-5d18-9712-69501b60ddc5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-50ebbed4-eb9c-5659-8b8c-f37f72666390" :answer-field/id #uuid "50ebbed4-eb9c-5659-8b8c-f37f72666390"] ["answer-f308dd20-f66e-5ffb-861b-4ab8333e47b2" :answer/id #uuid "f308dd20-f66e-5ffb-861b-4ab8333e47b2"] ["answer-f308dd20-f66e-5ffb-861b-4ab8333e47b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f308dd20-f66e-5ffb-861b-4ab8333e47b2" :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3\\pi}"] ["answer-field-50ebbed4-eb9c-5659-8b8c-f37f72666390" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-50ebbed4-eb9c-5659-8b8c-f37f72666390" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-50ebbed4-eb9c-5659-8b8c-f37f72666390" :answer-field/correct "answer-f308dd20-f66e-5ffb-861b-4ab8333e47b2"] ["answer-field-50ebbed4-eb9c-5659-8b8c-f37f72666390" :answer-field/choices "answer-f308dd20-f66e-5ffb-861b-4ab8333e47b2"] ["question-14280c74-af6e-5d18-9712-69501b60ddc5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-50ebbed4-eb9c-5659-8b8c-f37f72666390"] [17592186221445 :knowledge-point/questions "question-14280c74-af6e-5d18-9712-69501b60ddc5"] ["question-e5dc675f-f1b9-58e9-a567-64d8cd60aaaf" :question/id #uuid "e5dc675f-f1b9-58e9-a567-64d8cd60aaaf"] ["question-e5dc675f-f1b9-58e9-a567-64d8cd60aaaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-341873"] ["question-e5dc675f-f1b9-58e9-a567-64d8cd60aaaf" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=2x+7$ for $x\\in [-3,3).$ The Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{1}.$\n\n${a}_{1}=$ {{field-1}}"] ["question-e5dc675f-f1b9-58e9-a567-64d8cd60aaaf" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and $f(x)=2x+7$ for $x\\in [-3,3).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(2x+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x+7\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{3}(uv\\,{|}_{-3}^{3}-{\\int }_{-3}^{3}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{3}{\\pi }{[(2x+7)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)]}_{-3}^{3}-{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{3}{\\pi }[13\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )]-\\frac{6}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot 0-\\frac{6}{\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{\\pi }){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}x)]}_{-3}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{18}{{\\pi }^{2}}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )]) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{\\pi }^{2}}(-1-(-1)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-e5dc675f-f1b9-58e9-a567-64d8cd60aaaf" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-2afc926f-9cf1-5b4f-8748-f140b3012b4a" :answer-field/id #uuid "2afc926f-9cf1-5b4f-8748-f140b3012b4a"] ["answer-96e025f6-a797-5f53-bd93-ef33e6a27f03" :answer/id #uuid "96e025f6-a797-5f53-bd93-ef33e6a27f03"] ["answer-96e025f6-a797-5f53-bd93-ef33e6a27f03" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-96e025f6-a797-5f53-bd93-ef33e6a27f03" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-field-2afc926f-9cf1-5b4f-8748-f140b3012b4a" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-2afc926f-9cf1-5b4f-8748-f140b3012b4a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-2afc926f-9cf1-5b4f-8748-f140b3012b4a" :answer-field/correct "answer-96e025f6-a797-5f53-bd93-ef33e6a27f03"] ["answer-field-2afc926f-9cf1-5b4f-8748-f140b3012b4a" :answer-field/choices "answer-96e025f6-a797-5f53-bd93-ef33e6a27f03"] ["question-e5dc675f-f1b9-58e9-a567-64d8cd60aaaf" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-2afc926f-9cf1-5b4f-8748-f140b3012b4a"] [17592186221445 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e5dc675f-f1b9-58e9-a567-64d8cd60aaaf"] ["question-8c3f231c-8d0c-511e-b4f9-0d81c5e6659f" :question/id #uuid "8c3f231c-8d0c-511e-b4f9-0d81c5e6659f"] ["question-8c3f231c-8d0c-511e-b4f9-0d81c5e6659f" :question/math-academy-id "q-341863"] ["question-8c3f231c-8d0c-511e-b4f9-0d81c5e6659f" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=x+1$ for $x\\in [-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{2}.$\n\n${a}_{2}=$ {{field-1}}"] ["question-8c3f231c-8d0c-511e-b4f9-0d81c5e6659f" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and $f(x)=x+1$ for $x\\in [-2,2).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+1\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(uv\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\pi }{[(x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)]}_{-2}^{2}-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\pi }[3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-(-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )]-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\pi }){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)]}_{-2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot 0+\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2\\pi )]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-8c3f231c-8d0c-511e-b4f9-0d81c5e6659f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-a7ebfbb0-eafe-5de9-be9a-5eb3748e9483" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7ebfbb0-eafe-5de9-be9a-5eb3748e9483"] ["answer-88ed5bbc-d47f-5994-8b20-ac726fec6a85" :answer/id #uuid "88ed5bbc-d47f-5994-8b20-ac726fec6a85"] ["answer-88ed5bbc-d47f-5994-8b20-ac726fec6a85" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-88ed5bbc-d47f-5994-8b20-ac726fec6a85" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-field-a7ebfbb0-eafe-5de9-be9a-5eb3748e9483" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-a7ebfbb0-eafe-5de9-be9a-5eb3748e9483" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-a7ebfbb0-eafe-5de9-be9a-5eb3748e9483" :answer-field/correct "answer-88ed5bbc-d47f-5994-8b20-ac726fec6a85"] ["answer-field-a7ebfbb0-eafe-5de9-be9a-5eb3748e9483" :answer-field/choices "answer-88ed5bbc-d47f-5994-8b20-ac726fec6a85"] ["question-8c3f231c-8d0c-511e-b4f9-0d81c5e6659f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a7ebfbb0-eafe-5de9-be9a-5eb3748e9483"] [17592186221445 :knowledge-point/questions "question-8c3f231c-8d0c-511e-b4f9-0d81c5e6659f"] ["question-46598e7e-81d3-578b-80cc-94d59f9707e8" :question/id #uuid "46598e7e-81d3-578b-80cc-94d59f9707e8"] ["question-46598e7e-81d3-578b-80cc-94d59f9707e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-341861"] ["question-46598e7e-81d3-578b-80cc-94d59f9707e8" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-4x$ for $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${b}_{2}.$\n\n${b}_{2}=$ {{field-1}}"] ["question-46598e7e-81d3-578b-80cc-94d59f9707e8" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi $ and $f(x)=-4x$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(-4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{\\pi }x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(-4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-4x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-4 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{2}{[(-4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))(-4)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{2}((-4\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-(4\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2\\pi ))-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{2}((-4\\pi )\\cdot 1-(4\\pi )\\cdot 1)-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(4\\pi -(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot (4\\pi -0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-46598e7e-81d3-578b-80cc-94d59f9707e8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-6c30a88d-8e13-5d71-9185-007060f3d4e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c30a88d-8e13-5d71-9185-007060f3d4e5"] ["answer-824395f4-e1d3-5e0f-879c-0d03e310d7a5" :answer/id #uuid "824395f4-e1d3-5e0f-879c-0d03e310d7a5"] ["answer-824395f4-e1d3-5e0f-879c-0d03e310d7a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-824395f4-e1d3-5e0f-879c-0d03e310d7a5" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-field-6c30a88d-8e13-5d71-9185-007060f3d4e5" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-6c30a88d-8e13-5d71-9185-007060f3d4e5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-6c30a88d-8e13-5d71-9185-007060f3d4e5" :answer-field/correct "answer-824395f4-e1d3-5e0f-879c-0d03e310d7a5"] ["answer-field-6c30a88d-8e13-5d71-9185-007060f3d4e5" :answer-field/choices "answer-824395f4-e1d3-5e0f-879c-0d03e310d7a5"] ["question-46598e7e-81d3-578b-80cc-94d59f9707e8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-6c30a88d-8e13-5d71-9185-007060f3d4e5"] [17592186221445 :knowledge-point/questions "question-46598e7e-81d3-578b-80cc-94d59f9707e8"]] "retractions" []}]